ok   /dev/null opens
ok   a read of it is at EOF
ok   a write of it is swallowed whole
ok   /dev/kmem opens
ok   the u-area reads back whole
ok   its u_uid is our uid
ok   its u_gid is our gid
ok   this image is impure, so virtual 0 is p_addr + USIZE
ok   u_procp names our proc entry
ok   our image lives above the unmapped reach
ok   /dev/mem opens
ok   both devices read the low words
ok   and they agree over the kernel's const segment
ok   a read crossing KREACH returns both words
ok   and its first word is the one kmem shows
ok   /dev/kmem ends at the unmapped reach
ok   /dev/mem ends at the end of core
ok   /dev/mem finds our own word above 0100000
ok   a write through /dev/mem reaches it
